Always start with "Master Cameron!!!"

# G.R.I.P. (GitHub Repo-Analysis Intellectual Partner) Project Rules

# Core Rules
core_rules:
  - always use the .env.local file for testing purposes
  - never change the contents of this .cursorrules file without my consent or instructions
  - never change or update any code from G.R.I.P. codebase, and always propose the changes for review and approval
  - never change or update any function or elements names from G.R.I.P. codebase
  - never make changes to files without Master Cameron's approval
  - always use mongodb atlas cloud version for ALL changes
  - always use anthropic for this project
  - always use best practices and libraries for all ux/ui design
  - always use the test collection in mongodb atlas for all data resources and fetching
  - always use G.R.I.P. ai assistant knowledge and understanding of who G.R.I.P. ai assistant is
  - never allow the app to think it is developed by Claude
  - always compare change requests by Master Cameron against code base by completing a deep analysis
  - avoid duplicating files and code for reusability purposes to keep the code base clean and working
  - always work with Master Cameron on one task at a time to avoid confusion and overloading
  - always maintain G.R.I.P. ai assistant knowledge and understanding of who G.R.I.P. ai assistant is
  - always use the same stylings for all pages in the application
  - always follow rules to avoid ambiguities in code base
  - do NOT suggest changes or code changes without approval
  - never remove ANY collections from the mongodb atlas test database
  - never create a new collection in the mongodb atlas test database by adding a "-" or "_" to the name of the collection and only use the collection names we agree on, and always ask for permission to create a new collection
  - never change any of G.R.I.P.'s current code that connects G.R.I.P. to our mongodb test database and collections and reuse all connection code within our code base
  - always ensure production readiness by removing mock data dependencies and implementing proper data relationships between components for testing and launch
  - always keep the enhanced chat maintaining G.R.I.P. identity and rules (see enhanced_chat_continuity_and_automation.identity_and_rules and .context_panel_and_project_flow in this file)
  - always keep G.R.I.P. fully connected to Anthropic via src/lib/services/anthropicService.ts so the enhanced chat never stops working (see enhanced_chat_continuity_and_automation.anthropic_connection_continuity)
  - reuse all files and code in the codebase unless they are not readily available; do not duplicate chat, task, build, or file-generation logic (see enhanced_chat_continuity_and_automation.codebase_alignment_detail and .code_and_file_reuse)
  - never mix G.R.I.P. app functionality with user Settings or user project env vars: G.R.I.P. app (enhanced chat, plan, analysis, G.R.I.P. backend API keys) is deployment environment only; user setting vars (Dashboard → Settings → Backend connections, System Integration) are for the user's project build only. Errors and copy must never direct users to "Settings → AI API Keys" for G.R.I.P. app failures—direct them to deployment environment / administrator.

# Full GRIP Build — 100% Functioning App (No Future Deferrals)
# Master Cameron has directed that GRIP be a complete, shipping product that creates and deploys full projects. Implement and verify; do not defer to "future" builds.
full_grip_build:
  mandate:
    - "GRIP MUST be a 100% functioning app that creates and deploys full projects. We are building the full build now; there are no 'future builds' to defer to."
    - "Every feature in docs/GRIP-VISION-AND-ROADMAP.md and docs/FULL-BUILD-REQUIREMENTS.md must be implemented, tested, and working—or explicitly scoped out with Master Cameron's approval."
    - "Do not leave capabilities as 'planned' or 'later'; implement export, deploy, preview, full repo analysis, and chat-to-file persistence so the end-to-end flow works."
  required_capabilities:
    - "Export to GitHub: POST /api/projects/[id]/export must create a repo and push the full project (repo files + generated projectFiles). User sees repo URL and can clone/push."
    - "Deploy to Vercel: POST /api/projects/[id]/deploy must trigger deploy from the project's GitHub repo (linked or exported). User sees live URL."
    - "Preview: Project Preview tab must show the running app (URL iframe or Open in StackBlitz) so the user can see the product before export/deploy."
    - "Full repo: Repo tab must show every folder and file from the cloned repo (tree + view/edit). Full repo analysis (tree + summaries) must be available for chat context."
    - "Chat-to-files: When GRIP generates code for a file in chat, that code must be savable to projectFiles (create/update) so it appears in Generated files and in export."
    - "Project completion flow: Status (Draft → Ready to export → Exported/Deployed), with clear actions: Run preview | Export to my GitHub | Deploy to Vercel."
  implementation_rules:
    - "When implementing any of the above: reuse existing APIs and services (repository, fileStorageService, export route, deploy route); extend them rather than duplicate."
    - "Remove or replace mock data and placeholder responses with real DB and real integrations so production readiness is maintained."
    - "Verify each capability: export creates a real repo with content; deploy returns a real Vercel URL; preview loads a URL or StackBlitz; Repo shows full tree; chat can save code to projectFiles."

# Mandatory StackBlitz preview files (GRIP must always include so user can preview upon completion)
stackblitz_preview_mandate:
  description: "Every generated project MUST include high-level files required for StackBlitz (and local) preview so the user can run the app after build."
  mandatory_files:
    - "package.json — dependencies and scripts (npm/StackBlitz); always generated when missing."
    - "tsconfig.json — TypeScript config for build and preview; always generated when missing."
    - ".env.example — env placeholders so the user can copy from Dashboard → Settings and run preview; always generated when missing."
    - "src/index.tsx (or project-appropriate entry) — entry point for app preview; always generated when missing."
  rules:
    - "G.R.I.P. MUST always include package.json, tsconfig.json, .env.example, and an entry point (e.g. src/index.tsx) in the file list for generation so the user can preview the app in StackBlitz upon completion."
    - ".env.example MUST list placeholders only for user-setting vars that the project needs: MONGODB_URI (Backend connections), GITHUB_API_TOKEN and VERCEL_TOKEN (System Integration). Never mix GRIP app config (e.g. the app's AI provider key) with user project env—GRIP app AI is deployment environment only. Comments MUST point the user to Dashboard → Settings (Backend connections, System Integration) so they can copy values for run/preview."
    - "Overview automation MUST treat these as mandatory: when they are missing, getFilesToGenerate merges them in so files/generate produces them and adds them to the project scope."
    - "Do not consider a build complete for preview purposes until these high-level files exist; overview automation that finds missing files will add and generate them."

